%description:

Tcp.initialCwnd:segments -- the first flight has this number of segments.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the initial congestion window in segments, in place of initialWindow,
as the initcwnd of a Linux route".

The classes: zero (0, the default: initialWindow decides), segments (1 and more), invalid
(below 0). The code: TcpAlgorithmBase::getInitialWindow(), and the check in
TcpConnection::configureStateVariables(). This test separates "segments" from "zero".

Host under test: host1, with 5, which sends 30000 bytes. Observation: level 1, the data segments that host1 sends before the first ACK of data comes
back: the links have a delay of 10 ms, so the round trip is 40 ms, and a full-sized segment
has 1448 bytes.

%# parameter: Tcp.initialCwnd
%# class: segments
%# value: 5
%# key: *.host1.tcp.initialCwnd
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpInitialCwndSegments")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .meanwhile(anyNumberOfTimes(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                                        .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
                                        .captureCount("flight")
                                        .describe("each data segment of host1")
                                        .within(2.0)))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && tcp.ackBit == true && tcp.ackNo > {isn} + 1")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("{flight} == 5")
             .describe("the first ACK of data, after 5 data segments")
             .within(1.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpInitialCwndSegments compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.initialCwnd = 5    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 30000B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpInitialCwndSegments: PASS
